 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 518427,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "If $7,500 is deposited in a 4-year CD earning 3.28% interest compounded monthly, how much is in the account after 4 years?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The future value of an investment, <i>A</i>, when the principal, <i>P</i>, is invested at an annual interest rate of <i>r</i> (in decimal form), compounded <i>n</i> times per year for <i>t</i> years is found using the formula <span data-math=\"A = P{\\left( {1 + \\frac{r}{n}} \\right)^{nt}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><i>Hint</i>: Find <i>nt</i> before you plug numbers into your calculator!</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"nt = \\left( {12} \\right)\\left( 4 \\right) = 48\"></span></p>\n<p>It will help you get the right results. Use those parentheses in your calculator, too!</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = 7,500{\\left( {1 + \\frac{{0.0328}}{{12}}} \\right)^{40}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = \\$ 8,549.93\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$8,549.93"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
